# Finance Visual Concepts v1

## Visual Principles

| # | Principle | Visual implication |
| - | --------- | ------------------ |
| V1 | **Case is the canvas** | Primary viewport = one interpreted Financial Case, not a spreadsheet of entities |
| V2 | **Interpretation before chrome** | Verdict + owner + lane occupy the “hero” of the case; entity details are supporting |
| V3 | **Reading, not badge theater** | Verdict looks like an explanation block, not a lone colored pill that replaces facts |
| V4 | **Ownership gates the action rail** | Action cluster appears only after owner is visible; disabled/absent when not finance’s move |
| V5 | **Calm > alarm for expected states** | Coexistence and correct waiting use neutral/informational tone, not error red |
| V6 | **Signals are secondary surfaces** | Attention lists are narrow, dismissible, or side-rail — never the whole product metaphor |
| V7 | **Progressive depth** | L1 always on; L2–L5 expand without burying L1 |
| V8 | **Altitude change is obvious** | Exception/audit modes change frame treatment (banner/mode chip), not just extra tabs |
| V9 | **Universal skeleton, local flesh** | Layout slots are **U**; labels/urgency widgets are **Ad/D** |
| V10 | **No repair-by-default** | Manual payment / create-intent never dominates the visual hierarchy as “fix unpaid” |

**Marks:** **U** reusable · **Ad** adapter · **D** Denali-only  
**Probes:** **A** enrollment+offline · **B** subscription+recurring · **C** marketplace order  

---

## Case Canvas Concept

### Metaphor

A **case dossier** for one commercial subject: who it is, how money reads right now, whose move, what you may do.

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  CASE CANVAS (primary)                                  │
│  L1: identity · verdict reading · owner · lane · alarm  │
│  L2: facts that explain the reading                     │
│  L3: confidence                                         │
│  L4: action rail (allow/forbid)                         │
│  L5: history / audit (collapsed by default in daily)    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
         ↑ opens from
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  SIGNAL RAIL / INDEX (secondary)                        │
│  pending evidence · unsettled · exception · audit cues  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### Not the canvas

Payment table · receipt inbox-as-app · ledger browser · registration list-as-finance-home.

### Multi-workspace

Canvas structure = **U**. Subject header fields = **Ad**. **D** tour/member labels only in Denali binding.

---

## Information Hierarchy Visualization

### L1 — Immediate understanding (always visible on Case canvas)

| Appears | Why | Hidden until needed |
| ------- | --- | ------------------- |
| Subject identity (name + product title) | Anchor | Raw UUID unless identity missing |
| Verdict **reading** (short title + one-sentence narrative) | “Where are we?” | Full fact dump |
| Owner line (“Next move: finance / counterparty / …”) | Whose move | Action buttons before this |
| Lane indicator (daily / exception / audit) | Altitude | Audit panels |
| Alarm treatment (neutral vs caution) | Coexistence health | Error styling by default |

**Visual weight:** L1 is the densest “above the fold” block — explanation-first, not toolbar-first.

### L2 — Facts supporting interpretation (visible, secondary density)

| Appears | Why | Hidden until needed |
| ------- | --- | ------------------- |
| Eligibility | Money path open? | Product lifecycle action controls |
| Policy (money due / not) | Chase vs no-chase | Implementation of policy editors |
| Obligation / remaining | Amount judgment | Ledger lines |
| Evidence progress | Ingress | Full file viewer until review |
| Intent summary | Open/captured | Manual create form |
| Settlement meaning | Projection | Sync/debug tooling |

**Visual weight:** Definition list / compact fact grid under L1; each fact object-qualified.

### L3 — Ownership / confidence (adjacent to L1 or directly under)

| Appears | Why | Hidden until needed |
| ------- | --- | ------------------- |
| Why visible | Confidence | — |
| Why mine / not mine | Confidence | — |
| If I wait… | Calm waiting | Fear copy |
| Avoid… | Forbidden set preview | Full forbid list dump |

Prefer one progressive ownership story (L1 headline + L3 detail), not two competing owner widgets.

### L4 — Actions (rail or footer of case)

| Appears | Why | Hidden until needed |
| ------- | --- | ------------------- |
| Primary posture CTAs from allow set | Act / wait / escalate / inspect | Row kebab menus as primary |
| Explicit wait affordance when wait is correct | Success outcome | Fake “must click something” |
| Forbidden actions not shown as primary; optional “why not” | Clarity | Tempting repair CTAs |

### L5 — History / audit (collapsed in daily)

| Appears | Why | Hidden until needed |
| ------- | --- | ------------------- |
| Prior evidence decisions | Retry context | Always-open ledger |
| Intent history | Duplicate detection | — |
| Lifecycle timeline (**Ad**) | Eligibility story | Finance lifecycle buttons |
| Ledger / recon | Audit only | Daily default open |

**Rule:** Expanding L5 never steals L1–L4 hierarchy.

---

## Signal → Case Transition

### Signal presentation (secondary)

Conceptual treatments (not components):

| Signal type | Visual cue concept | Priority cue |
| ----------- | ------------------ | ------------ |
| Pending evidence | “Needs finance reading” in signal rail | Count + age; **Ad** service-window urgency |
| Unsettled obligation | “Needs interpretation” — not “fix payment” | Must not look like finance-owned until Case opens |
| Exception | Distinct caution mode chip on signal | Higher than calm unsettled |
| Audit finding | Audit altitude chip | Never default home |

### Transition

```text
Select signal
  → Case canvas replaces or overlays signal as focus
  → L1 populated before L4 actions
  → Signal item remains breadcrumb (“from: evidence needing review”)
```

### Queues remain secondary

| Do | Don’t |
| -- | ----- |
| Narrow rail / split list→detail where detail is Case | Full-viewport receipt table as the product |
| Label lists as attention indexes | Title the product “Receipts” as finance home |
| Empty signal rail still allows Case search/open by subject (**Ad**) | Force all work through one entity inbox |

### Avoid

“Finance inbox = receipt list.”

### Multi-workspace

Signal taxonomy = **U**. Which signals dominate = **Ad** (A: evidence; B: failed charge; C: unpaid order / dispute).

---

## Verdict Visualization

### Concept: “Interpretation card” not “status badge”

Visual idea:

- **Title:** human reading (e.g. “Awaiting finance review”)  
- **Supporting sentence:** object-qualified narrative  
- **Linked facts:** chips or links into L2 slots (evidence, settlement) — facts still reachable  
- **Tone:** informational for expected states; caution only for EXCEPTION / unhealthy alarm  

### Examples

| Verdict | Visual reading concept | Tone |
| ------- | ---------------------- | ---- |
| `AWAITING_COUNTERPARTY` | Waiting on counterparty — money due, no evidence in finance hands | Calm |
| `AWAITING_FINANCE` | Evidence with finance — unsettled projection expected | Calm / in-progress (not error) |
| `SETTLED_CAPTURED` | Settled after accepted capture/evidence | Positive calm |
| `NO_MONEY_DUE` | No payment chase | Calm complete |
| `NOT_ELIGIBLE` | Money path not open — product desk | Calm / handoff |
| `EXCEPTION` | Commercial meaning unclear — pause routine acts | Caution mode |

### Rules

- Verdict is a **reading**, not a stored status control  
- Avoid single-color-pill mentality that hides narrative  
- Do not let settlement badge alone sit where verdict should sit  

### Multi-workspace

Presentation pattern = **U**. Wording = **Ad/D**.

---

## Ownership Visualization

### Concept: “Next move” strip

Always visible in L1/L3:

| Owner | Visual distinction concept |
| ----- | -------------------------- |
| `counterparty` | Outbound wait — “their move” |
| `finance` | Inbound work — “your move” |
| `product_desk` | Handoff — “product ops move” |
| `policy_system` | System/policy — “no human money chase” |
| `exception_policy` | Exception mode — “judgment required” |
| `idle` | Complete — “no money action” |

### Action coupling

- If owner ≠ `finance` (and not exception requiring finance cleanup): action rail emphasizes **Wait** / handoff, not approve  
- If owner = `finance`: approve/reject (when allowed) become primary  
- Never imply ownership merely because the operator is on a “finance” route  

### Multi-workspace

Owner set = **U**. Labels (member/subscriber/buyer) = **Ad/D**.

---

## Decision Interaction

### Action rail concept

Sourced only from `allowedActions` / `forbiddenActions` (+ owner/lane).

| Posture | Visual concept |
| ------- | -------------- |
| **Act now** | Primary button group for allowed finance decisions (e.g. approve/reject evidence) |
| **Wait** | Explicit “Correct to wait” control or confirmed idle state — not a disabled void |
| **Escalate** | Secondary/caution control when exception lane |
| **Inspect** | Tertiary / mode switch into audit altitude |

### Avoid

- Row action menus as the main decision UX  
- Payment-first CTAs (“Create manual payment”) as default above-the-fold  
- Manual payment as default repair for unpaid/waiting  
- Showing approve when owner is counterparty  

### Multi-workspace

Postures = **U**. Dominant primary CTA = **Ad**.

---

## Waiting Experience

### Goal

Waiting communicates **correctness**, not failure.

### Visual treatments

| Situation | Visual concept |
| --------- | -------------- |
| Eligible, counterparty pending | Calm wait panel: owner=counterparty; no error color; “if you wait = delay only” |
| No money due | Complete/idle calm; no evidence queue pull |
| Lifecycle not ready | Handoff to product_desk; finance actions absent |
| Settled idle | Quiet success; no further CTA noise |

### Coexistence vs wait (visual)

| State | Who acts | Visual |
| ----- | -------- | ------ |
| Evidence in review + unsettled | **Finance** | In-progress calm (Pattern coexistence) — **not** “waiting empty” |
| No evidence + unsettled + eligible | **Counterparty** | True calm waiting |

### Avoid

Error red, “failed sync,” pulsing unpaid alarms, forced create-payment CTA.

---

## Exception/Audit Experience

### Exception mode

Case canvas gains:

- Mode banner: “Exception — commercial meaning unclear” + trigger reason  
- Routine approve/reject **suppressed** or behind confirm-with-reason  
- Owner shifts to `exception_policy` visual  
- L2 highlights conflicting slots  

### Audit mode

- Mode banner: “Audit altitude”  
- L5 ledger/recon expands as **supporting investigation**  
- Findings map back to L2 fact callouts (settlement vs intent vs evidence)  
- Exit returns to daily Case reading  

### Keep secondary

Ledger tables, journal lines, recon boards — never replace L1 verdict/owner.

### Multi-workspace

Mode transformation = **U**. Which triggers fire = **Ad**.

---

## Responsive Considerations

Conceptual breakpoints (not CSS):

| Viewport | Concept |
| -------- | ------- |
| **Wide** | Signal rail + Case canvas side-by-side; L1–L4 stacked in case; L5 collapsed |
| **Medium** | Signal list → Case full width on select; sticky L1 summary |
| **Narrow** | Signal index as first step; Case as full-screen dossier; action rail sticky bottom; L2 accordion; L5 behind “More / Audit” |

**Mobile rule:** Never open entity row actions without Case L1. Sticky owner + primary posture beat dense tables.

**Signal rail on small screens:** One-dimensional list of attention items; detail is always Case.

